      "source_context": "Therefore, a mature summer-bearing raspberry planting has two types of canes: vegetative canes that originated during the current year (primocanes) and fruiting canes that originated during the previous year (floricanes). Fruit is usually harvested in mid-summer. Everbearing (also referred to as primocane-fruiting or fall-bearing) raspberries produce primocanes that are capable of flowering and fruiting in the same year they emerge.",
